   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div>Seems like I&#39;m missing something about how stat_ellipse works. I have this data:</div><div><br></div><div><table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"256\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:192pt\">\n <colgroup><col width=\"64\" span=\"4\" style=\"width:48pt\">\n </colgroup><tbody><tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\n  <td height=\"20\" width=\"64\" style=\"height:15.0pt;width:48pt\">speaker</td>\n  <td width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\">vowel</td>\n  <td width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\">F1</td>\n  <td width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\">F2</td>\n </tr>\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">test</td>\n  <td>i</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">240.75</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">2841.7</td>\n </tr>\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">test</td>\n  <td>i</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">240.58</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">2828.25</td>\n </tr>\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">test</td>\n  <td>i</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">243</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">2850.12</td>\n </tr>\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">test</td>\n  <td>e</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">501.75</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">2292</td>\n </tr>\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">test</td>\n  <td>e</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">481.5</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">2214</td>\n </tr>\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">test</td>\n  <td>e</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">490</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">2200</td>\n </tr>\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">test</td>\n  <td>a</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">661.5</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">1156.4</td>\n </tr>\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">test</td>\n  <td>a</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">665.9</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">1167.8</td>\n </tr>\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">test</td>\n  <td>a</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">662</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">1165</td>\n </tr>\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">test</td>\n  <td>o</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">510.75</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">994.5</td>\n </tr>\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">test</td>\n  <td>o</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">511</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">988</td>\n </tr>\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">test</td>\n  <td>o</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">510.75</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">967.5</td>\n </tr>\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">test</td>\n  <td>u</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">238</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">629</td>\n </tr>\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">test</td>\n  <td>u</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">249.75</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">630</td>\n </tr>\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">test</td>\n  <td>u</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">236.25</td>\n  <td align=\"right\">627.75</td>\n </tr></tbody></table><br></div><div>and running this code:</div><div>ggplot(data = df, aes(x = F2, y = F1, color = vowel)) + geom_point() + stat_ellipse()<br></div><div><br></div><div>and getting the error message:</div><div>Error: Discrete value supplied to continuous scale<br></div><div><br></div><div>Note, that when I run the code without &quot;color=vowel&quot;, it draws an ellipse just fine, and running the code here: <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/15100130/fill-superimposed-ellipses-in-ggplot2-scatterplots\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/15100130/fill-superimposed-ellipses-in-ggplot2-scatterplots&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792372065923000&amp;usg=AOvVaw30Jm7V8D9nUeGFL5YA1V2C\">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/15100130/fill-superimposed-ellipses-in-ggplot2-scatterplots</a> I get the plot just like in the image.</div></div>"
