  {
   "id": "eM9RhDtSP2IJ",
   "from": "Brandon Hurr",
   "author": "27405c4b711a1080",
   "date": "2013-09-25T07:44:54Z",
   "subject": "Re: stat_ellipse Discrete value supplied to continuous scale",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Not entirely sure, but it looks like stat_ellipse() has an issue with computing an ellipse when you have less than 4 values per subset of your data. In your case each level of &quot;vowel&quot; only has 3 points. <div>\r\n\r\n<br></div><div>From the github page: </div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px\">dfd </span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;font-weight:bold\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px\"> length</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px\">data</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;font-weight:bold\">$</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px\">x</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;font-weight:bold\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;color:rgb(0,153,153)\">1</span></div>\r\n\r\n<div><pre style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">if</span> <span>(</span>dfd <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">&lt;</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,153,153)\">3</span><span>){</span></div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;padding-left:10px\">ellipse <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">&lt;-</span> rbind<span>(</span>c<span>(</span><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">NA</span><span>,</span><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">NA</span><span>))</span></div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;padding-left:10px\"><br></div><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">If you supply it with a bigger dataset it works fine.</font><br>\r\n\r\n</pre><pre style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></pre><pre style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">ggplot(data = df, aes(x = F2, y = F1, colour = speaker)) + geom_point() + stat_ellipse()<br>\r\n\r\n</font></pre><pre style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></pre><pre style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">My best guess. </font></pre>\r\n\r\n<pre style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></pre><pre style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">HTH, B</font></pre></div></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
