    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Wednesday, September 25, 2013 2:44:54 AM UTC-5, Brandon Hurr wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Not entirely sure, but it looks like stat_ellipse() has an issue with computing an ellipse when you have less than 4 values per subset of your data. In your case each level of &quot;vowel&quot; only has 3 points. <div>\r\n\r\n<br></div><div>From the github page: </div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px\">dfd </span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;font-weight:bold\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px\"> length</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px\">data</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;font-weight:bold\">$</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px\">x</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;font-weight:bold\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;color:rgb(0,153,153)\">1</span></div>\r\n\r\n<div><pre style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">if</span> <span>(</span>dfd <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">&lt;</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,153,153)\">3</span><span>){</span></div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;padding-left:10px\">ellipse <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">&lt;-</span> rbind<span>(</span>c<span>(</span><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">NA</span><span>,</span><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">NA</span><span>))</span></div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;padding-left:10px\"><br></div><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">If you supply it with a bigger dataset it works fine.</font><br>\r\n\r\n</pre><pre style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></pre><pre style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">ggplot(data = df, aes(x = F2, y = F1, colour = speaker)) + geom_point() + stat_ellipse()<br>\r\n\r\n</font></pre><pre style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></pre><pre style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">My best guess. </font></pre>\r\n\r\n<pre style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></pre><pre style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">HTH, B</font></pre></div></div>\r\n\r\n<div><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Sep 25, 2013 at 1:06 AM, Daniel Scarpace <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">daniel....@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div>Seems like I&#39;m missing something about how stat_ellipse works. I have this data:</div><div>\r\n<br>\r\n</div><div><table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"256\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:192pt\">\r\n <colgroup><col width=\"64\" span=\"4\" style=\"width:48pt\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" width=\"64\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt;width:48pt\">speaker</td>\r\n  <td width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\">vowel</td>\r\n  <td width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\">F1</td>\r\n  <td width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\">F2</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">test</td>\r\n  <td>i</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">240.75</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2841.7</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">test</td>\r\n  <td>i</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">240.58</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2828.25</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">test</td>\r\n  <td>i</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">243</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2850.12</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">test</td>\r\n  <td>e</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">501.75</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2292</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">test</td>\r\n  <td>e</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">481.5</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2214</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">test</td>\r\n  <td>e</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">490</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2200</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">test</td>\r\n  <td>a</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">661.5</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">1156.4</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">test</td>\r\n  <td>a</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">665.9</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">1167.8</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">test</td>\r\n  <td>a</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">662</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">1165</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">test</td>\r\n  <td>o</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">510.75</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">994.5</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">test</td>\r\n  <td>o</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">511</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">988</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">test</td>\r\n  <td>o</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">510.75</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">967.5</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">test</td>\r\n  <td>u</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">238</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">629</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">test</td>\r\n  <td>u</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">249.75</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">630</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15.0pt\">test</td>\r\n  <td>u</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">236.25</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">627.75</td>\r\n </tr></tbody></table><br></div><div>and running this code:</div><div>ggplot(data = df, aes(x = F2, y = F1, color = vowel)) + geom_point() + stat_ellipse()<br></div><div><br></div><div>and getting the error message:</div>\r\n\r\n<div>Error: Discrete value supplied to continuous scale<br></div><div><br></div><div>Note, that when I run the code without &quot;color=vowel&quot;, it draws an ellipse just fine, and running the code here: <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/15100130/fill-superimposed-ellipses-in-ggplot2-scatterplots\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/15100130/fill-superimposed-ellipses-in-ggplot2-scatterplots&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792372065930000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3SwCIK9DHm4YPKN-3afl7J\">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/15100130/fill-superimposed-ellipses-in-ggplot2-scatterplots</a> I get the plot just like in the image.</div>\r\n\r\n</div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.<br>\r\nPlease provide a reproducible example: <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792372065930000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3i3hTvHaavGUMOV6PIXNTg\">https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility</a><br>\r\n <br>\r\nTo post: email <a rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nTo unsubscribe: email <a rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nMore options: <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" da